.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Ginzburg and Landau described superconductivity with a free-energy functional of a complex order parameter alone, no microscopic pairing mechanism required. Minimizing it gives an equilibrium condensate density |\psi_0|^2=-a/b (~physicskit.condensed.ginzburg_landau.gl_equilibrium_order_parameter) below the transition, and two length scales -- the coherence length \xi (~physicskit.condensed.ginzburg_landau.gl_coherence_length) and the penetration depth \lambda (~physicskit.condensed.ginzburg_landau.gl_penetration_depth) -- whose ratio, the Ginzburg-Landau parameter \kappa (~physicskit.condensed.ginzburg_landau.ginzburg_landau_parameter), alone decides Type I vs Type II behavior.">

